{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-327582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nfor some function $f(x,y).$ The table below shows the intermediate quantities computed in the first iteration of the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nGiven that the step size is $Δx=\\frac{1}{4},$ at which of the following points is the function $f$ evaluated during this iteration?\n\n- $(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{2})$\n- $(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{4})$\n- $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{8})$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042033/state.json" "file_sha256" "e91f0265fbb56bac6f3defd32391a6887b7137fe74160344893f525a71cb361b"} {"question" "q-327582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the estimated slope at the initial point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{′}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{′}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{′}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the estimated slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$\n\nNow, we have the following table of values:\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{2}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{3}^{′}\\,$ | $Δy$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |\n\nWith this in mind, let's find each point at which the slope is evaluated in turn using the values given in the table.\n\n- The slope ${y}^{′}$ is evaluated at the initial point $(x,y)=({x}_{0},{y}_{0})=(0,1).$\n\n- The estimated slope ${y}_{1}^{′}$ is evaluated at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{1},{y}_{1}) & =(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The estimated slope ${y}_{2}^{′}$ is evaluated at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{2},{y}_{2}) & =(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4},\\,1+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8},\\frac{3}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The estimated slope ${y}_{3}^{′}$ is evaluated at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{3},{y}_{3}) & =(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx) \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{1}{4},\\,1+(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4},\\frac{3}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, of the given options, the slope is evaluated at the points \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042033/state.json" "file_sha256" "e91f0265fbb56bac6f3defd32391a6887b7137fe74160344893f525a71cb361b"} {"question" "q-327582" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042033/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d91913132f5ad8ddbab789466955116612609a5b8d0d1ce1f7a4da1b009d6a4d"} {"question" "q-327582" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/